A.1.14. {"problem": "The new `deployed` precondition on `verify` allows any request at stage `built`, without checking `harness_ok`. A built request whose harness failed (fixture R2: built, harness_ok false) passes the precondition. Verifying it then leaves a verified request with neither `deployed` nor `harness_ok`, which violates the relaxed invariant `verified-requests-were-deployed`. The rule that a dry run needs a passing harness is therefore not enforced where the action is checked.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, actions.verify precondition `deployed` vs invariant `verified-requests-were-deployed`", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
A.1.15. {"problem": "A dry-run verification moves a built request to `verified`. In that state `preview`, `deploy` and `record_deployment` are `n/a` and `verify` is denied as 'Already verified'. A request that has been dry-run verified can never be deployed or previewed again. That defeats the purpose of verifying before deploy, and the request would have to be re-created through a new handoff.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, transitions.DeliveryRequest.matrix.verified and built.verify", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.1.16. {"problem": "The glossary entry for `verified` still says 'A deployment a person has checked in use, after it happened'. The success metric counts versions that reach 'verified-in-use'. The invariant id `verified-requests-were-deployed` and the precondition id `deployed` also now describe something the rules no longer require. A dry-run verification makes `verified` mean 'nothing was deployed', which inflates the metric. The `verify` description itself still says it confirms the deployed domain via the probes, and a dry run has nothing deployed to probe.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, glossary.verified, purpose.success_metric, invariant id `verified-requests-were-deployed`, precondition id `deployed`", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.1.17. {"problem": "The diff marks the changed `verify` action, its precondition, the `built.verify` transition and the two relaxed invariants as `status: proposed`. In the files after the change they all show `status: confirmed`, and the precondition and invariants no longer carry a quote. The `built` to `verified` transition and the two relaxed invariants would therefore be deployed as confirmed, although no person has confirmed them. The relaxed invariants also drop their previous confirmed interview source and cite only an unquoted `interview.jsonl#L28`.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, actions.verify, transitions built.verify, invariants verified-requests-were-deployed and finished-deploys-record-the-outcome", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.1.18. {"problem": "The behaviour of `verify` changes (it now works from `built`, and the invariants are looser), but the delivery domain `version` stays at 4. No scenario covers a dry-run verify, and no scenario covers the rejection of a built request with a failed harness. A scenario for the second case would have exposed the harness gap in the precondition.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, version and scenarios", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
